# GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 — 2× DGX Spark (GB10 / SM121)
# Copy to .env and edit. ./start.sh does this for you on first run.
# Caller exports override this file, including explicit empties (KEY= ./start.sh).

# --- nodes (edit these) ------------------------------------------------
HEAD_IP=10.0.0.1
WORKER_IP=10.0.0.2
# SSH user on the worker. Unset = same as the user running ./start.sh.
# Only set this when the worker account differs (e.g. WORKER_USER=zurih).
# WORKER_USER=
# WORKER_HOME=/home/zurih
# WORKER_SSH=zurih@10.0.0.2

# Direct CX7 QSFP (spark1 f1 ↔ spark2 f0 on this kit). NCCL cannot use the
# 10.0.0.x loopback aliases — without these pins ncclCommInitRank hangs.
# Other kits: names differ (e.g. enP2p1s0f1np1/roceP2p1s0f1 on both nodes of
# some Spark pairs) — list yours with `ls /sys/class/infiniband` + `ip -br a`.
# These per-node values are what the containers get; exporting generic
# NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME / NCCL_IB_HCA does NOT override them.
HEAD_CX7_IF=enp1s0f1np1
WORKER_CX7_IF=enp1s0f0np0
HEAD_CX7_IB=rocep1s0f1
WORKER_CX7_IB=rocep1s0f0
# The RoCEv2 GID index is per-NIC: each node needs the index carrying its OWN
# ::ffff:<ip> entry. An all-zero entry kills that rank ~60 s in (ibv_modify_qp
# errno 61); preflight verifies each rank against its own device. Inspect:
#   cat /sys/class/infiniband/<dev>/ports/1/gids/{0..7}
# If one index works on both nodes, set NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX. If the nodes need
# different indices (e.g. head 4 / worker 3), set them per rank instead —
# both default to NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX when unset.
# NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX=2
# HEAD_GID=4
# WORKER_GID=3

# --- weights -----------------------------------------------------------
# Durable public mirror (same bytes as brandonmusic snapshot 5ab363a8).
# If that Hub id 404s, start.sh downloads MODEL_FALLBACK instead.
MODEL=Mia-AiLab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-TR3-4bpw
MODEL_FALLBACK=brandonmusic/GLM-5.3-Flash-tr3-4bpw
# Already downloaded the upstream id on this kit? Uncomment so we do not
# re-fetch 164 GiB into a second cache folder:
# MODEL_CACHE_NAME=models--brandonmusic--GLM-5.3-Flash-tr3-4bpw
# Optional: pin a Hub commit on the mirror (empty = branch default).
MODEL_REVISION=25a44fdbf16862a46b7cc9921142c6c81350af2f
# HF cache root on the head (worker uses ${WORKER_HOME}/.cache/huggingface)
# HF_HOME=/home/you/.cache/huggingface
# HF_TOKEN=hf_xxx
# HF CLI override when `hf` lives outside PATH (venv installs). May contain
# arguments. Without it start.sh falls back to `python3 -m
# huggingface_hub.commands.huggingface_cli` when huggingface_hub is importable.
# HF_BIN=/home/you/.hf-cli/venv/bin/hf

# --- serve -------------------------------------------------------------
# Public GHCR image. ./start.sh docker-pulls this on the head, then on
# the worker if that node can reach GHCR; otherwise docker save
# --platform | ssh docker load. No login required.
# Overlay rebuild from this repo: BUILD=1 ./start.sh
# start.sh also rebuilds once when Dockerfile/overlay change after git pull
# (recipe stamp). Keep a pulled GHCR tag: SKIP_BUILD=1
# Skip the pull (use whatever is already local): SKIP_PULL=1
# Skip copying to the worker: SKIP_SHIP=1
# Force the ~164 GiB rsync even when the worker revision marker matches:
# FORCE_SYNC=1
# Local-only tag (no pull): IMAGE=glm53-flash-sm121:local
IMAGE=ghcr.io/miaai-lab/glm-5.3-flash-2x-dgx-sparks:exl3
# GHCR_USER=MiaAI-Lab
# GHCR_TOKEN=ghp_xxx
PORT=8888
TP=2
NNODES=2
MASTER_PORT=29521
QUANTIZATION=exl3
# 0 = CUDA graphs. 1 = eager. start.sh adds capture sizes: DFlash2
# 1 2 4 8 16 24 32, MTP 1 2 3 4 6 8 12 (must include 3).
ENFORCE_EAGER=0
# 1 = fused exllamav3_ext.exl3_moe per layer; 0 = unique-expert LinearEXL3 loop
EXL3_FUSED_MOE=1
# 1 = GPU 128-row tiles for fat prefill experts; 0 = LinearEXL3 fallback
# EXL3_MOE_ROW_TILE=0
# Fused temp rows/expert. 1024 lost the MNBT=1024 A/B (P2b); keep 128.
# EXL3_TEMP_ROWS_FUSED=32   # launcher default: 32 with E3 (EXL3_FAT_GROUPED=1), 256 with E2
# Sorted routing tier; 0 falls back to legacy scans unless a higher tier is on.
# EXL3_FAT_SORTED=0
# E1 batched tier: persistent scratch + combined gate/up; implies SORTED=1.
# EXL3_FAT_BATCHED=0
# E2 direct kernel (default on). Implies BATCHED=1 and SORTED=1.
# Needs the patched extension — start.sh rebuilds when the overlay recipe drifts.
# EXL3_FAT_KERNEL=0 restores the legacy fat-expert path without a rebuild.
EXL3_FAT_KERNEL=1
# E3 grouped fat-expert kernels: one gather + gate/up + down launch per layer for
# every fat expert from device-side tables, no host sync. +37-45% cold prefill on
# this kit (README "Cold prefill (E3)"). Default 1 since 2026-09-07. Needs an image
# with the exl3_fat_moe kernels (./start.sh rebuilds on recipe drift; fails closed
# at load without them). The launcher picks EXL3_TEMP_ROWS_FUSED=32 for E3 and 256
# for E2 unless set. Set 0 for the E2 kernel path (then 1M context fits again).
EXL3_FAT_GROUPED=1
SERVED_MODEL_NAME=GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3

# Winner on this 2× GB10 kit with DFlash2: fused MoE + DFlash2 k=7.
# Draft KV is auto/bf16; the target still uses KV_CACHE_DTYPE=fp8 (fp8_ds_mla).
# Rollback: SPEC_METHOD=mtp
SPEC_METHOD=dflash
DFLASH_MODEL=incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2
# Exact checkpoint behind the published 2026-08-30 TP=2 receipts.
# Override with an exact commit; empty follows the cached main ref (refresh to update).
DFLASH_REVISION=dc77ff1c99eeb2df044ee3d4f0094eb033fee410
DFLASH_TOKENS=7
# Drafter TP. 2 = measured keep on this 2× GB10 kit (shard draft across ranks).
# 1 = rank 0 only (skip CX7 on a 2.3 GiB draft). Empty = inherit TP.
DFLASH_DRAFT_TP=2
MTP_TOKENS=2

# --- decode speed-ups from the 2026-09-08 overnight run (both default OFF) ---------------
# Adaptive verification length (overlay/patch_adaptive_k.py): the drafter keeps its 7-token
# block, the scheduler verifies only a per-step prefix (2, 4 or 7) chosen from a per-request
# EMA of accepted draft tokens, batch-uniform so FULL CUDA graphs still run. Lossless at temp 0.
# Prose +13-21 % per stream (hard essays most, counting unchanged). Needs the capture-size
# list below (multiples of 3, 5 and 8 up to 4 requests).
# GLM53_ADAPTIVE_K=ema
# GLM53_ADAPTIVE_K_SET=2,4,7
# Marlin FP8 weight-only for the KDA + dense-MLP projections (overlay/patch_dense_fp8.py):
# ~-11 ms per decode step (+10 % on everything, prose +12-19 % alone, +37 % on hard prose
# stacked with adaptive-k). PROVISIONAL: changes target numerics by FP8 rounding (KL proxy vs
# stock 0.002-0.013 nats/position; no full KLD panel yet). Groups: shared,dense,kda,mla.
# GLM53_DENSE_FP8=dense,kda
# The graph list adaptive-k needs, plus a KV-pool cap so FP8's freed GPU memory becomes host
# headroom instead of a bigger pool (uncapped, the head dropped to ~1.5 GiB MemAvailable at 850k).
# 14 GiB leaves a 883,552-token pool = 1.04x of MAX_MODEL_LEN 850000 and ~5 GiB host headroom;
# 15 GiB (16106127360) gives 1.11x but measured only 0.8-2.2 GiB free under load. Do not go much
# lower at 850k: the boot refuses a pool that cannot hold one max-length request (13 GiB = ~820k).
# Stock launcher capture-size default is "1 2 4 8 16 24 32".
# EXTRA_ARGS="--cudagraph-capture-sizes 1 2 3 4 5 6 8 9 10 12 15 16 20 24 32 --kv-cache-memory-bytes 15032385536"
# Tuning (defaults shown): GLM53_ADAPTIVE_K_ALPHA=0.25 GLM53_ADAPTIVE_K_MARGIN=1.0
# GLM53_ADAPTIVE_K_MIN_STEPS=4 GLM53_ADAPTIVE_K_SATURATE=max GLM53_ADAPTIVE_K_HIST=200
# Runtime override without a reboot: <CACHE_ROOT>/glm53_adaptive_k.json ({"mode","set","margin",...}).
# Booting from a git worktree: ablit/transplant must be a real copy, not a symlink (see README).
MAX_MODEL_LEN=850000
MAX_NUM_SEQS=4
# Prefill chunk. Current maintainer default at MAX_NUM_SEQS=4: 7168.
# On an independent MAX_NUM_SEQS=16 geometry, 2048 gave the best measured
# throughput/KV balance. Re-run 2048 vs 7168 before changing; never 8192
# (indexer smem).
MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS=7168
# Empty = stock scheduler (no --long-prefill-token-threshold flag).
# Measured A/B/A at MNBT=7168 with LONG_PREFILL_TOKEN_THRESHOLD=3584 (MNBT/2):
# warm-session freeze 131/108 s stock -> 15 s; contended prefill +6%;
# solo prefill +3..+11%, within baseline drift. Re-measure for other kits.
# Positive integer <= MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS, or empty.
LONG_PREFILL_TOKEN_THRESHOLD=
GPU_MEM_UTIL=0.85
KV_CACHE_DTYPE=fp8
# 0 = load vision tower (image + video). 1 = language-only.
LANGUAGE_MODEL_ONLY=0
# Skip max-size dummy MM profile at init (that OOM'd this UMA). Keep 1 with vision.
SKIP_MM_PROFILING=1
# Per-prompt multimodal ceiling. Validation only — nothing is reserved for it, because
# SKIP_MM_PROFILING=1 skips the max-size dummy profile. The real bound is the context
# window: this processor emits 16-8000 tokens per image, so ~100 large images can fill
# MAX_MODEL_LEN on their own and an over-long prompt is rejected as too long anyway.
# Exceeding this cap returns HTTP 500 "At most N image(s) may be provided in one prompt",
# so keep it generous; lower it if you want prompts refused early instead.
LIMIT_MM='{"image":100,"video":1}'

# --- abliteration (optional, default off) -----------------------------------
# ABLIT=1 edits self_attn.o_proj at weight-load (overlay/ablit_runtime.py).
# Artifacts in ablit/ come from
# drowzeys/keys-GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4-ablit-l15-45-anchorstock (published
# "dealign-oproj-transplant": layers 15-45 edited, 0-14 stay stock safety
# anchors, MTP block included). Restart to toggle; no rebuild needed.
ABLIT=0
# auto = transplant when ablit/transplant/ is populated, else proj
ABLIT_METHOD=auto
# dealign (published recipe) | bf_oproj | absolute path to a custom direction .pt
ABLIT_DIRECTION=dealign
# Inclusive layer range. 45 is the checkpoint MTP block (used when it loads).
ABLIT_LAYERS=15-45
# W' = (I - alpha * r r^T / ||r||^2) W. 1.0 = plain projection;
# 3.0 = published alpha_ref (over-projects — stronger, less coherent).
ABLIT_ALPHA=3.0
# Also edit the MTP block's o_proj when it is loaded (SPEC_METHOD=mtp).
ABLIT_INCLUDE_MTP=1

# --- API auth --------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAI-compatible bearer token. vLLM reads the VLLM_API_KEY env var natively
# (fallback when --api-key is absent on the CLI), so the key never lands in
# argv / the `non-default args` startup log. Empty = unauthenticated.
# Same single-key semantics as the DeepSeek V4 Flash DSpark deployment.
# VLLM_API_KEY=

# --- JIT caches / boot warmup ----------------------------------------------
# Overlay ~/.triton and ~/.tilelang die on container recreate. These host
# dirs are bind-mounted to /root/.triton/cache and /root/.tilelang/cache.
# TRITON_HOST_CACHE=
# TILELANG_HOST_CACHE=
# After /health, burn DFlash2 BLOCK / sampler / kpool shapes so TP=2 does
# not JIT mid-collective. 0 = skip (nonfatal either way).
GLM53_BOOT_SHAPE_WARMUP=1
# GLM53_WARMUP_REQ_TIMEOUT=240
# Suppress client stop strings until </think> (thinking-on default). 0 = off.
GLM53_SUPPRESS_STOPS_IN_REASONING=1
# When a decode seq is running, do not mix a peer prefill into that step
# (issue #6). skip = decode-only steps; N>0 = cap mixed prefill tokens; 0 = off.
GLM53_MIXED_PREFILL_CHUNK=skip
# Server default: empty (no flag), low, high, or max. Empty preserves the
# template's Max fallback for omitted effort; medium is not a template level.
# Example opt-in: GLM53_DEFAULT_REASONING_EFFORT=high
# Per-request chat_template_kwargs.reasoning_effort overrides this default.
GLM53_DEFAULT_REASONING_EFFORT=
# Sparse-indexer prefill gather workspace sizing.
#   stock     = max_model_len * 40 entries (5036.40 MB locked at 1M, measured)
#   rightsize = the legal per-step maximum, ~+26% KV cache. Opt-in.
# See docs/DESIGN-indexer-workspace.md. Anything else is rejected at launch.
GLM53_INDEXER_WORKSPACE=rightsize
# SpinCondition reader busy-loop window: stock keeps vLLM's 1 s default;
# 1..1000 selects milliseconds. This deployment's frozen sweep selected 16.
GLM53_SPINWAIT_MS=stock
# EngineCore execute timeout (seconds). Stock 300 is short for a cold JIT.
# VLLM_EXECUTE_MODEL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=1800

# Host NCCL preload. Default off: the glm53-flash image already has nvidia-nccl,
# and LD_PRELOAD of a second SO makes DeepEP assert duplicate NCCL.
USE_HOST_NCCL=0
# NCCL_HOST_DIR=/home/you/nccl-2.30.7
# WORKER_NCCL_HOST_DIR=/home/you/nccl-2.30.7
NCCL_SO_NAME=libnccl.so.2.30.7
NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX=3
# vLLM deducts a CUDA-graph memory estimate from the KV pool. Where the estimate
# exceeds what the graphs actually use, 0 returns that memory to KV with graphs
# still enabled. 1 = upstream default.
CG_ESTIMATE=1
NCCL_DEBUG=WARN

# Per-group APC retention for the DFlash2 drafter SWA group. Empty inherits the
# global policy; 0 keeps reachable boundaries only; N must be a multiple of
# 3584. The global interval (VLLM_PREFIX_CACHE_RETENTION_INTERVAL) stays unset.
# TP=2 only; start-tp4.sh rejects a non-empty value.
GLM53_APC_RETENTION_INTERVAL_SWA=
